WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.630
Hello, everyone! I'm Mr. Jake. Welcome to Online A two, Book one.

2
00:00:04.930 --> 00:00:08.212
Hi! I'm Sreypich. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.512 --> 00:00:15.576
Unit twenty-four: Clubs and Teams. In this unit, you will talk about clubs and teams with the present perfect.

4
00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:17.271
Club.

5
00:00:17.971 --> 00:00:20.458
Club means a group that meets to do an activity.

6
00:00:20.758 --> 00:00:22.108
I'm in the English club.

7
00:00:22.808 --> 00:00:24.984
Your turn. Say: Club.

8
00:00:27.684 --> 00:00:28.290
Club.

9
00:00:29.283 --> 00:00:29.901
Team.

10
00:00:30.601 --> 00:00:33.425
Team means a group of people who play or work together.

11
00:00:33.725 --> 00:00:35.376
Our team has twelve players.

12
00:00:36.076 --> 00:00:38.706
Your turn. Say: Team.

13
00:00:41.406 --> 00:00:42.012
Team.

14
00:00:43.017 --> 00:00:43.844
Member.

15
00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:47.089
Member means a person who belongs to a group.

16
00:00:47.389 --> 00:00:49.133
I'm a member of the chess club.

17
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:51.870
Your turn. Say: Member.

18
00:00:54.570 --> 00:00:55.397
Member.

19
00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:57.129
Coach.

20
00:00:57.829 --> 00:00:59.945
Coach means a person who trains a team.

21
00:01:00.245 --> 00:01:02.082
Our coach is strict but kind.

22
00:01:02.782 --> 00:01:05.202
Your turn. Say: Coach.

23
00:01:07.902 --> 00:01:08.752
Coach.

24
00:01:09.750 --> 00:01:10.693
Practice.

25
00:01:11.393 --> 00:01:13.311
Practice means a time when you train.

26
00:01:13.611 --> 00:01:15.286
We have practice twice a week.

27
00:01:15.986 --> 00:01:18.580
Your turn. Say: Practice.

28
00:01:21.280 --> 00:01:22.200
Practice.

29
00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:23.941
Match.

30
00:01:24.641 --> 00:01:27.290
Match means a game between two teams.

31
00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.288
We have a match on Saturday.

32
00:01:29.988 --> 00:01:32.071
Your turn. Say: Match.

33
00:01:34.771 --> 00:01:35.610
Match.

34
00:01:36.617 --> 00:01:37.467
Join.

35
00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.888
Join means to become a member.

36
00:01:40.188 --> 00:01:42.071
I have joined the volleyball team.

37
00:01:42.771 --> 00:01:45.667
Your turn. Say: Join.

38
00:01:48.367 --> 00:01:49.067
Join.

39
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:50.981
Captain.

40
00:01:51.681 --> 00:01:53.565
Captain means the leader of a team.

41
00:01:53.865 --> 00:01:55.272
She is the team captain.

42
00:01:55.972 --> 00:01:58.207
Your turn. Say: Captain.

43
00:02:00.907 --> 00:02:01.757
Captain.

44
00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:04.633
Now let's listen to a conversation.

45
00:02:04.933 --> 00:02:07.885
Sreypich, have you joined a club this year?

46
00:02:09.183 --> 00:02:11.603
Yes! I have joined the volleyball team.

47
00:02:12.917 --> 00:02:14.719
How many matches have you played?

48
00:02:16.017 --> 00:02:17.749
We have played three matches.

49
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.005
Have you won?

50
00:02:21.317 --> 00:02:24.120
We have won two. And I have become captain!

51
00:02:25.417 --> 00:02:28.705
Grammar focus: Present perfect (I have joined ).

52
00:02:29.005 --> 00:02:31.889
I have joined the team. We have won two matches.

53
00:02:32.189 --> 00:02:37.826
Use the present perfect for experiences and news without a time. Use 'has' with he, she or it.

54
00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:41.492
Now read and listen. Our Volleyball Team.

55
00:02:41.792 --> 00:02:44.128
I'm a member of the school volleyball team.

56
00:02:45.417 --> 00:02:48.171
Our coach is strict, and we have practice twice a week.

57
00:02:49.483 --> 00:02:51.738
This year, we have played four matches.

58
00:02:53.050 --> 00:02:54.574
We have won three of them!

59
00:02:55.883 --> 00:02:59.520
Last month, I became captain, and I'm very proud.

60
00:03:00.817 --> 00:03:03.411
Quiz time! Choose the correct answer.

61
00:03:03.711 --> 00:03:05.188
I blank joined the team.

62
00:03:05.488 --> 00:03:08.398
A, have. B, has. C, am.

63
00:03:12.383 --> 00:03:14.754
The answer is A: have.

64
00:03:16.250 --> 00:03:17.843
We have blank two matches.

65
00:03:18.143 --> 00:03:21.030
A, win. B, won. C, wins.

66
00:03:25.017 --> 00:03:26.865
The answer is B: won.

67
00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.152
The leader of a team is the blank.

68
00:03:30.452 --> 00:03:33.757
A, captain. B, member. C, match.

69
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.645
The answer is A: captain.

70
00:03:41.150 --> 00:03:44.917
Now it's your turn to speak. Which club or team would you like to join?

71
00:03:50.217 --> 00:03:55.017
I would like to join the drama club. My friend has joined it, and she says it's fun.

72
00:03:55.317 --> 00:03:57.549
Excellent answer, Sreypich!

73
00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:04.407
Great work today! You learned eight new words and present perfect (i have joined ).

74
00:04:04.707 --> 00:04:08.520
Today's value is teamwork. We can do more when we work together.

75
00:04:08.820 --> 00:04:12.390
See you in Unit twenty-five. Goodbye!

76
00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:15.063
Thank you, Mr. Jake! Bye, everyone!

